 "needs": [
  {
   "kind": "speech_act",
   "text": "Introduce new mathematical operations.",
   "source": [
    "t1:s1"
   ],
   "id": "n1",
   "context": "Consider the following new operations: $a # b$ equals $(2 + b) - a$ if $a > b$ and $b$ otherwise. $a ][ b$ equals $(a - b)$ if $a + b > 0$; otherwise,  it equals $a + b$. $a ; b$ equals $(b # a) - b$ if $|a-b| < 2$ and $(a # b) - a$ otherwise. $a @ b$ equals $(a ][ a) - b$ if $b < 2$ and $(b ][ b) - a$ otherwise. $a ~ b$ equals $(a ; b)$ if $a - b > 0$; otherwise,  it equals $a # b$. For brevity, we use $a <op1><op2> b$ to denote $(a op1 b) op2 b$. For example, $4 +* -5$ means $(4 + -5) * -5$ and $4 *-- -5$ means $(4 * -5) -- -5$. Let A = (((((((((((((((((((2 ~- -8) *~ 5) ][~ -3) # -9) *+][ 4)",
